# The same proof with every base the identity.
#
# Algorithm 10.7 types the bases as "G_q^n", and the identity is a
# member of G_q.  The "\ {1}" that the same document puts on the
# Schnorr base is absent here, so a base vector of all ones is
# type-correct input.  Then phi is the constant map: every witness
# has the same image, the honest image is all ones, and the proof
# demonstrates nothing whatever about x.
secrets x
claims  x
eq  1   1
eq  1   1
eq  1   1

# This statement names no base but the identity, so there is
# nothing for an environment to get wrong: the instance check
# has no input and the verdict is about the statement alone.
